o Kottke y sus excursiones de guitarra, John Hartford, Norman Blake, Michael Hurley (el mejor discípulo del acid-folk de los Holy Modal Rounders), el «jazzgrass» de David Grisman (con Tony Rice y Mark O'Connor) y el improvisador Eugene Chadbourne.","color":"#a3e635","family":"Folk y cantautores","link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#newgrass"}],"book_tracks":[{"id":8284360544851,"artist":"David Grisman","artist_id":49289259010420,"title":"The David Grisman Quintet","year":1977,"ess":1,"yt":"ICUSsmu7FWg","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Bluegrass progresivo y jazzgrass","scene_id":278336191326907,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#newgrass","chapters":["Sección 4.2"],"pages":[[1,81,null]]},{"id":279637104291386,"artist":"David Grisman","artist_id":49289259010420,"title":"Hot Dawg","year":1979,"ess":0,"yt":"Evn1b300S6o","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Bluegrass progresivo y jazzgrass","scene_id":278336191326907,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#newgrass","chapters":["Sección 4.2"],"pages":[[1,81,null]]},{"id":15564693960390,"artist":"David Grisman","artist_id":49289259010420,"title":"Quintet '80","year":1980,"ess":0,"yt":"btnpT_9p-58","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Bluegrass progresivo y jazzgrass","scene_id":278336191326907,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#newgrass","chapters":["Sección 4.2"],"pages":[[1,81,null]]}],"mentions":[{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":81,"text":"…growl and haphazard guitar picking, and his cohort Jeffrey Frederick (1), whose Spiders In The Moonlight (1977) is no less heretical. In 1976 David Grisman (3) coined \"jazzgrass\", a fusion of jazz and bluegrass. Grisman had experimented with jazz and country on Earth Opera's The Great American Eagle Tragedy (1969), mostly arranged by Peter Rowan, and on the historical session of Muleskinner (1974), featuring both Rowan and Greene of Seatrain. The David Grisman Quintet (1977), featuring guitarist Tony Rice, was the album that Stephane Grappelli in person played on Hot Dawg (1979) and Grisman perfected his line-up on Quintet '80 (1980): Darol Anger on violin, Mike Marshall on mandolin, Mark O'Connor on guitar, and Bob Wasserman on…"},{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":203,"text":"…ensemble with albums such as Shadowdance (1983). Significant contributions to the \"chamber\" wing of new-age music came from former members of David Grisman's quintet, whose \"jazzgrass\" lent itself to a neo-classical interpretation. Violinist Darol Anger, pianist Barbara Higbie, mandolinist Mike…"},{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":320,"text":"…fanzine for punk-rock and new-wave music ？ Pere Ubu cut Modern Dance, possibly the greatest new-wave album ？ Richard Hell cuts Blank Generation ？ David Grisman coins \"newgrass\", a fusion of jazz and bluegrass ？ Wanted: The Outlaws, featuring Waylon Jennings, Willie Nelson, Tompall Glaser and Jessi Colter,…"}],"podcast":[],"awards":[],"concerts":[],"xref":[],"charts":[{"id":200651322761745,"type":"album","name":"The David Grisman Rounder Album","list_id":276702392435984,"list":"RYM Top — Country — Bluegrass","src":"musthear","rank":150,"year":1976,"note":null,"yt":"Z3miWWlFSLI","scaruffi":null},{"id":200651322761745,"type":"album","name":"The David Grisman Rounder Album","list_id":238825082427763,"list":"RYM Top — Country — Progressive Bluegrass","src":"musthear","rank":102,"year":1976,"note":null,"yt":"Z3miWWlFSLI","scaruffi":null},{"id":8284360544851,"type":"album","name":"The David Grisman Quinte